# nr-relay-hook: the webhook tunnel of mixdog-relay (native/core/crates/mixdog-relay): src/hook/{mod,leg,http}.rs, tests/hook.rs
# Nothing here could be compiled (no cargo in this task).

## 1. Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, mixdog-workspace-hack, compose_flip.rs SERVICE_PENDING
No change. tests/hook.rs is picked up as the test target `hook` (the crate does not turn auto-discovery off) and needs no
test-support item. Every dependency used (base64, bytes, serde_json, uuid, thiserror, tokio sync, httparse, mixdog-rt, mixdog-js) is
already a dependency of the crate. No protocol method is registered.

## 2. src/lib.rs
`pub mod hook;` is already there.

## 3. What the tasks that run the relay (nr-relay-server, nr-relay-legs-phone sweep) must apply
- One `hook::HookHub` per process: `HookHub::new(pool.clone(), HookOptions { max_pending: <maxHookPending option, default 64>,
  ingress: <the server's legIngress numbers with limit = 1 MiB (IngressLimits::hook() carries the defaults)>, ..Default::default() })`,
  the same `IngressPool` the desktop and phone legs use. The hub owns the caller limiter (`hookLimiter`, 120 per 60 s per `device:<id>` and
  per `ip:<ip>`), so server/start.rs builds no hook limiter.
- router.rs: a request whose target starts with `/hook/` goes to `hub.handle_request(request, response).await` (it answers every case
  itself: 400, 404, 429, 503, 413, 504, 502 and the agent's answer).
- upgrade.rs, `/hookleg`: authenticate exactly as `/desktop` does (authenticateLeg: routing id, secret of 16 characters or more, register
  limiter for unknown ids, `auth:<ip>` limiter for failures; the raw 401/429 refusals), then `WebSocketServer::handle_upgrade`, then
  `tokio::spawn(async move { hub.run_leg(&device_id, socket, events).await })`. `run_leg` installs the ingress tap itself (before the first
  event), supersedes an earlier leg of the device (closed 4000 "superseded", its parked requests fail 502), and releases the ingress leg
  and fails the parked requests when its socket closes. The hub does not authenticate: it takes the device id the upgrade code settled.
  The http1 connection type must be a `ws::Transport` (nr-relay-http1 / nr-relay-ws wire).
- The 10 s sweep covers hook legs too: for each `leg` of `hub.legs()` run the ingress branches first (`leg.ingress().sweep(now)`: Closed and
  Parked move on), then the ping window with `leg.is_alive()` / `leg.set_alive(false)` and `leg.socket().ping(..)` (the pong and every
  message of the agent set it again inside `run_leg`). A leg superseded and closing 4000 is no longer listed; the socket's own 30 s close
  timeout destroys it.
- close(): after the sweep and the sockets are stopped, `hub.fail_pending_and_clear()` (closeRelay's failHookPending over liveHooks,
  then clear).
